# ChimeraX structure preparation and mutagenesis template
# For use with AlphaFold3 protein-DNA complex output
# Replace YOURFILE.pdb with your actual AF3 output filename
# Replace chain letters and residue numbers to match your system

# Open and inspect the structure
open YOURFILE.pdb
color bfactor #1 palette alphafold
info chains #1

# Confirm chain layout matches expectation before proceeding
# Typical layout for a homodimer-DNA complex:
#   Chain A -- protein monomer 1
#   Chain B -- protein monomer 2
#   Chain C -- DNA sense strand
#   Chain D -- DNA antisense strand

# Clean the structure
delete solvent
delete :UNK

# Verify key residues are present and positioned near DNA
# Replace residue numbers below with your actual contact residues
select :RES1,RES2,RES3
show sel atoms

# Save the wild type structure
save WT/PROTEIN_WT_clean.pdb format pdb


# Mutagenesis: substitute target residues with alanine
# Replace chain letters and residue numbers to match your system
# Run swapaa one residue at a time and confirm each before continuing

swapaa ala #1/A:RES1
swapaa ala #1/A:RES2
swapaa ala #1/A:RES3

# If the complex is a homodimer, apply the same substitutions to chain B
swapaa ala #1/B:RES1
swapaa ala #1/B:RES2
swapaa ala #1/B:RES3

# Verify mutations in the sequence panel before saving
# Each target position should now show ALA
select #1/A:RES1,RES2,RES3
show sel atoms

# Save the mutant structure
save MUT/PROTEIN_MUT_clean.pdb format pdb


# Notes:
# swapaa can fail silently on residues near chain termini or in tightly packed regions.
# Always verify in the sequence panel that the substitution applied correctly.
# If a swap fails, rerun that single swapaa command individually and check again.
#
# After saving, check both PDB files for:
#   - Correct TER records between chains
#   - DNA chains ordered after protein chains (required by tleap)
#   - No solvent or UNK residues remaining
#
# Before running tleap, strip the 5' phosphate atoms from the first residue
# of each DNA chain if present (OP3, P, OP1, OP2 on residue 1 of chains C and D).
# AF3 sometimes adds a 5' phosphate that is not included in tleap terminal templates.
# Use the following to remove them in ChimeraX before saving:
#
#   delete #1/C:1@OP3,P,OP1,OP2
#   delete #1/D:1@OP3,P,OP1,OP2
